<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2. </span>Characteristics of Rust-SWE-bench</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rust-SWE-bench provides 500 high-quality, manually reviewed task instances from 34 repositories, making it considerably larger and more diverse than other existing Rust SWE benchmarks like SWE-bench Multilingual <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khandpur et al., 2025</a>)</cite> (43 instances from 7 repositories) and Multi-SWE-bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib97" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zan et al., 2025</a>)</cite> (239 instances from 10 repositories). To ensure broad functional coverage, Rust-SWE-bench incorporates diverse project domains as shown in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.1.5. Manual verification ‣ 3.1. Benchmark Construction ‣ 3. Rust-SWE-bench ‣ Evaluating and Improving Automated Repository-Level Rust Issue Resolution with LLM-based Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, including command-line utilities (e.g., <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ripgrep</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gallant, 2024</a>)</cite>, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fd</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peter, 2024</a>)</cite>), development tools (e.g., <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cargo-edit</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">killercup, 2024</a>)</cite>, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">biome</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">BiomeJS, 2024</a>)</cite>), concurrency and parallelism libraries (e.g., <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tokio</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">The Tokio Authors, 2024b</a>)</cite>, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">rayon</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">The Rayon Developers, 2024</a>)</cite>), web frameworks (e.g., <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">axum</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">The Tokio Authors, 2024a</a>)</cite>), and specialized engines (e.g., <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bevy</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">The Bevy Community, 2024</a>)</cite>, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">boa</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">The Boa Developers, 2024</a>)</cite>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>. </span><span id="S3.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Overall Statistics of the Rust-SWE-bench</span></figcaption>
